{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ופרצים</b> — [You] shall make breaches in the wall." "<b>אשה נגדה, והשלכתנה</b> — Their end, namely the son, toward the mountain, so that they will not see the time of breaking out, as in the manner of 'and she cast the child.' Or from the severity of famine and thirst, as is written after it. Perhaps the Harmonah is the name of a place beyond the wall of Samaria. Now I have made known to you this evil destined to come upon you; therefore go, serve Baal—perhaps he will save you, in the manner that Elijah mocked his worshippers. And do not bring out the tithe at the end of three years—only for three days."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:59.628308274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}